    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the owner response that is `true` when more than 80 owners share the owner's registration day, otherwise `false`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` (boolean, `readOnly`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter. It's transient (never persisted); it's a per-response derived value, so MapStruct maps it into `OwnerDto` automatically by name (no mapper change needed).\n\n3. **`AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning.java`** \u2014 a new one-method function step that counts owners sharing the loaded owner's `registrationDate` (the same per-day accumulation used by `EnsureDailyCreateLimit`) and sets the flag to `count > 80`.\n\n4. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the step into both the create pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`, after `audit`/`save` so the new owner is counted) and the read pipeline (`{ownerId}.GET.yml`, after `load`), so the create response and a later GET compute the flag identically.\n\nThe daily-create-limit rule already rejects at \u2265100/day, so the >80 warning threshold sits below it on the same counting path. The acceptance test (`coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`) passes: a fresh create returns `bulkSignupWarning: false`, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
